From: Tang Nano 9K QERV <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] vt: 4 virtual consoles instead of 63

With CONFIG_VT the kernel registers a tty device (sysfs + devtmpfs) for every possible
virtual console at boot; on the 42 MHz QERV core each costs ~40 ms, so the 63 of them made
chr_dev_init take 2.6 s. The board has one framebuffer console (fbcon on tty1, doc/video_plan.md)
and no keyboard, so 4 are plenty. Only kernels with CONFIG_VT see this.
---
--- a/include/uapi/linux/vt.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/vt.h
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
  * resizing).
  */
 #define MIN_NR_CONSOLES 1       /* must be at least 1 */
-#define MAX_NR_CONSOLES	63	/* serial lines start at 64 */
+#define MAX_NR_CONSOLES	4	/* serial lines start at 64; tang9k: 4, see the patch */
 		/* Note: the ioctl VT_GETSTATE does not work for
 		   consoles 16 and higher (since it returns a short) */
 
